From d25c4de0e2f4a784ec8e40b2a752797bfd4c01d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Phase II executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 19:37:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Phase II Rung 2 (core): ice-transport reactions, ice
 conserved to machine precision

Generates the ice-transport pseudo-reactions so ice mantles ride their grains
through coagulation, with the corrected encoding (design thread confirmed):

  J_i X + GRAIN_j  ->  w1 J_k1 X + w2 J_k2 X + GRAIN_j

per ORDERED non-overflow pair (i,j) and ice base X, where (k1,k2,w1,w2) are the
grain reaction's product bins and SAME eps weights (ice-follows-particle):
  * GRAIN_j is a weight-1 CATALYST product -- regenerated, net-zero depletion,
    identically-zero Jacobian row. (Without this it would be consumed a second
    time at ~theta ~ 1e5-1e6 x the grain rate and annihilate the grains.)
  * rate = BARE kernel K_ij (coag_kernel_bare), i.e. full K_ii on the diagonal,
    NOT the grain 1/2: the reactants J_i X and GRAIN_j are distinct and each
    depleted once, so the self-collision needs the full K_ii (the 1/2 is a
    grain-identical-reactant artifact). Both directions per pair transport the ice
    on bin i and on bin j; i==j is one reaction whose full-K_ii rate already
    accounts for both grains' ice.

Plumbing: counting split so grain reactions (unordered non-overflow pairs) are
sized before read_species and ice transport (ordered pairs x ice bases) is added
in get_array_sizes once the ice-base count is known; injection enumerates ice
bases from the expanded species list (J01* -> base) and fills names/weights/type;
rates replay the ordered-pair loop per base with the bare kernel. Ice-transport
reactions share COAGULATION_TYPE, so the existing element/charge-balance exemption
and the tiling/ordering all apply unchanged.

Fixture fix: tests/fixture_ice_transport now lists BASE grain species (GRAIN0,
GRAIN-) and lets read_species expand them per bin, exactly like ice (JCO). The
earlier explicit per-bin listing double-counted and produced duplicate + null
species slots; base-only gives a clean 15-species list (6 gas, 6 grain, 3 ice).

Validated on the 3-bin toy (all CO ice in bin 1 at t0, constant kernel):
  * GATE (a) total ice sum_k Y(J_k CO) conserved to 4.1e-16 (machine precision),
    ice correctly migrating bin1 -> bin2,bin3 as grains coagulate;
  * dust-mass sum_k m_k n_k still conserved to 1.9e-13 (grain coag intact -- the
    catalyst encoding does not perturb grains);
  * coagulation-OFF still byte-identical (jac_weight_check 13450, 1.8006e-3, 0).
  Identical under -O0 and -O2.

Next: permanent ice gate (a + retained dust-mass + ice early-slope rate gate that
pins the bare-K_ii factor); ice-IC machinery (area-weighted default + per-species
fractional override + coverage guard + round-trip); extend jac_weight_check to the
ice-transport product weights; scale to the fiducial grid.
